A||||4||Hiller||Broke 85 GT||||1||
Z||000000||Hiller||12-19-1999||11:23 AM||||Help! Several problems with 85 GT that I have owned for about 9 years now.<P>1. Windshield wipers will sometimes make 1 uncommanded sweep. This occurs randomly, when turn signals cancel, or when turn signals are used.<P>2. Idle will dip and almost die then come back up to normal idle.<P>3. Engine will sometimes die when slowing to make a low speed corner. Push into neutral and the car starts right back up with normal idle. (May be related to 2 above)<P>4. Engine will die after 20-30 seconds when started with the engine cold. Sometimes will start right back up, sometimes not until allowed to sit a while. While looking under the hood on one of the times it didn't start back up, I heard a click like a valve, relay, etc. might make if stuck and then became unstuck. I tried the car and it started right back up. I have since heard this click regularly when trying to troubleshoot this problem and on every occurance the car would start after I heard the click. I have yet to find the source of the click. When the engine reaches normal operating temperature, this problem goes away until the car is allowed to cool back down. This start and die circus happens everytime the car is started with a cold engine.<P>All of these are intermitant problems. The car is an 85 GT with 2.8 V-6 and automatic. Thanks in advance for any help. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||12:39 PM||||Here's what you need to do:  (follow these instructions exactly)  1. Give the car to me.  2.  Buy another car.  I will take on the frustration of dealing with these problems for you.  ( <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Aren't I a nice guy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||12-19-1999||12:40 PM||||First the easy one. The wiper switch in the steering wheel stalk is bad. This also happens in an S-10 we have at work. Its a common failure. <P>The wipers will also go intermittant if water gets into the wiper module on the bulkhead. I had my coolant changed by a dealer, and right after my wipers would come on once in while. There's a board in there that gets wet and shorts out. The problem went away after the coolant dried out. <P>For driveability, go through the check list. Tune-up items, vacuum leaks, etc. Always start with the easy, normal service stuff when trouble shooting.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||HF6582||12-19-1999||12:44 PM||||Hiller,<BR>I've had the problem with the starting like the one you have. Traced it down to the fuel pump relay.  Next time it happens listen for the clicking by your air cleaner canister.<P>Hope that helps<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||12-19-1999||07:55 PM||||There were a couple of causes for the "phantom wipes". The wiper motor was one of the main causes. My Ciera had this demon.<P>Idle dip could be several things, but I would start with the FP relay unless it revs up first and then dips. Then I would go with a vacuum leak.<BR>||||reg||1
